  "id": "Compound::DB00511 - Gene::481",
  "verbalization": "Acetyldigitoxin appears to interact with Atp1b1 through a shared pathway involving the sodium-potassium-exchanging ATPase. The evidence suggests that Acetyldigitoxin binds to Fxyd2, which is involved in potassium transport, and this interaction leads to participation in the potassium-transporting ATPase activity, which in turn is linked to Atp1b1. Additionally, Acetyldigitoxin also binds to Atp1b3, which participates in the sodium-potassium-exchanging ATPase activity, ultimately leading to the same final association with Atp1b1. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where Acetyldigitoxin modulates the activity of Atp1b1 through its interaction with Fxyd2 or Atp1b3, influencing the potassium transport function of Atp1b1. The consistent scores across the paths suggest a robust relationship, though the exact mechanism of how Acetyldigitoxin directly affects Atp1b1 remains to be fully elucidated.",
